  "question": "The news subscription service system operates as follows: The system allows users to subscribe to news via email. News information includes News ID and News Name. Subscription information includes Subscription Status, Creation Time, Modification Time, and the IP Address at the time of subscription. Users can update their subscription status or cancel their subscription at any time based on their needs.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0381\nCREATE TABLE `news` (\n  `news_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `news_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`news_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscription` (\n  `subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `news_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `subscription_status` enum('active','inactive') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `modification_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`subscription_id`),\n  KEY `news_id` (`news_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscription_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`news_id`) REFERENCES `news` (`news_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
